  "summary": "# Daily Health-Tech Digest – June 18, 2026\n\nThe regulatory environment is shifting notably, with the FDA reversing its stance on UniQure's Huntington's disease therapy and showing openness to Moderna's flu vaccine, signaling renewed flexibility in drug approvals. Simultaneously, antitrust enforcement is intensifying—the DOJ's swift settlement with OhioHealth is prompting hospitals to review their contracts, while the FTC and state attorneys general sued a major gender-affirming care professional organization. Several important infrastructure challenges are emerging: conflicting state laws are creating compliance headaches for health-tech developers, rural healthcare fragmentation is straining access, and decades of CMS underpayment are creating a two-tiered system. On the innovation front, healthcare M&A is surging driven by biopharma and medtech deals, ambient AI is moving from pilot to enterprise deployment at institutions like Houston Methodist, and telehealth is expanding mental health diagnoses across regions. Meanwhile, workforce development shows promise—an NIH-supported diversity program doubled undergraduates' odds of earning a Ph.D.—though cybersecurity remains a concern with Novo Nordisk facing data extortion threats.",
